# Physics catalog P5c: the CPU twin of p5_tree_gpu_settle_2000, the same
# steps and bounds with the repulsion on the CPU law
# (tree.html?nodes=2000&seed=7&links=none&gpu=off).
assert snap ready == true
assert snap canvas-nodes == 2000
click role:button Play physics
settle 2
assert snap physics-paused == false
click role:combobox Arrangement
settle 1
click role:option Free (physics alone)
settle 1
click role:button Apply arrangement
settle 1
assert snap layout == free
assert snap physics-law == spring.rapier
log-physics start
timing start settle-2000
settle 30
timing stop
log-physics after-30-frames
settle 90
log-physics after-120-frames
# The bounds both runs must meet: the CPU run's signature, two-sided so a
# broken device law (overlaps, spread shrinking, energy stalling or running
# away) fails. Measured on the CPU run of 2026-10-02 (0 overlaps, spread
# 1,075, energy 399,968 after 120 frames, still expanding). Unlinked bodies
# (links=none): a linked random graph packs into a jammed ball under Springs,
# where the CPU run itself overlaps by the thousand and the energy is chaotic.
assert snap layout-overlaps <= 0
assert snap layout-spread >= 1020
assert snap layout-spread <= 1130
assert snap physics-energy >= 200000
assert snap physics-energy <= 800000
assert snap physics-device == off
log p5 cpu settle 2000 receipt complete
